WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.312
Across Wrocław, bronze dwarves share poses
and props.

00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:07.750
Given a photograph, which individual statue
are we looking at?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.880
Meet Doppeldwarf-306.

00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.100
A frozen vision model turns each image into
a vector: a

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.288
numerical visual description.

00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:20.250
Cosine similarity compares these vectors.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.150
Similar directions suggest similar
appearance;

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.975
they do not prove identity.

00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:28.662
We rank each statue by its best reference
photograph, without

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:30.380
fine-tuning the model.

00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:32.825
Now add more candidates.

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:35.038
Do lookalikes overwhelm retrieval?

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:39.000
Instead of reporting one accuracy number, we
repeatedly sample larger

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.725
candidate pools, always keeping the correct
statue.

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:45.388
DINOv2 's accuracy falls slowly;

00:00:45.388 --> 00:00:47.012
CLIP 's falls faster.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.980
The curve is the result.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.625
Surely location solves this?

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:55.188
But nearby lookalikes survive a hard
geographic filter.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:59.062
In simulation, a soft distance bonus works
better.

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:02.712
Across 294 placed statues, DINOv2

00:01:02.712 --> 00:01:06.475
rises from 93.4 to 98.7

00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:09.947
percent for users twenty-five metres away.

00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:14.554
A new photographer brings different
viewpoints, backgrounds, and lighting.

00:01:14.554 --> 00:01:15.992
Accuracy drops.

00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:19.892
Fewer remaining reference photographs also
contribute to that drop.

00:01:19.892 --> 00:01:23.717
Learned geometric matching checks whether
local details line up,

00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.304
improving the ranking.

00:01:25.304 --> 00:01:29.347
Classical SIFT adds no measurable gain in
this comparison.

00:01:29.892 --> 00:01:33.654
Finally, high similarity need not mean a
known statue.

00:01:33.654 --> 00:01:37.254
Comparing the best two candidates exposes
ambiguity.

00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:40.617
This margin reduces false acceptance in the
research;

00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:44.747
the browser demo uses a separately measured
close-call hint.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:48.754
The lesson: test the pool, the place, and
the photographer.

00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:51.880
Explore the dataset, and try the identifier.
